// shader-differential - NAMED REGRESSION for sampler PARAMETERS on the
// general path (claude 2026-09-01 21:44): lowerTex sets the texture unit
// to 0 unconditionally, so every tex2D samples unit 0 and a two-texture
// shader reads the first texture twice while the container still reports
// sa = TEX0, sb = TEX1.  One shared image for every sampler paints this
// correctly by construction; the per-name permuted images do not.
//
// Shape: q3_fp_modulate2's tex * tex (the two-sampler form the default
// matcher accepts), samplers as ordinary main() PARAMETERS - no file-scope
// anything - with sa at TEXCOORD0 and sb at TEXCOORD2 so the product is
// asymmetric.  Each name gets its own image (sa = perm FNV(sa) mod 24,
// sb likewise; the stager prints them).
//   correct:   sa-image(tc0) * sb-image(tc2)
//   unit 0 x2: sa-image(tc0) * sa-image(tc2)  - a different picture
// |both: the default path must stay identical (its units are right); the
// general path is RED today and green once the tex instruction carries
// the unit of the sampler it names, refusing when it cannot resolve one.
void main(
    float2 tc0 : TEXCOORD0,
    float2 tc2 : TEXCOORD2,
    uniform sampler2D sa,
    uniform sampler2D sb,
    out float4 oColor : COLOR)
{
    oColor = tex2D(sa, tc0) * tex2D(sb, tc2);
}
